  "deviations": [
    "High-contrast mode in DESIGN.md names only a subset of ColorToken. Missing tokens use the nearest existing high-contrast palette value: surfaces/sunken/overlay #000000, muted/faint #FFFFFF, secondary #000000, on-secondary #FFFFFF, border-strong #FFFFFF, primary hover/pressed #FFD400, selection #FFD400, scrim rgba(0,0,0,0.85). On-danger/on-success/on-warning are #000000.",
    "High-contrast focus ring is 3px (DESIGN.md); its offset is 2px, carried from the light/dark rule. High-contrast border width is 2px.",
    "High-contrast elevation shadows are none; 2px borders separate surfaces (DESIGN.md high-contrast border width is 2px and no shadow values are specified).",
    "Theme.elevation returns one Shadow (API.md fixed shape); tokens.json stores every CSS layer. The generated Theme uses the first layer: Low 0/1/2, Medium 0/4/8, High 0/12/24.",
    "DESIGN.md gives no numeric spring stiffness/damping/mass. tokens.json records Spring = 220ms with the ease-in-out curve and parameters:null; P1.5 must not invent a second spring token set.",
    "High-contrast chart tokens reuse the high-contrast palette (Chart1 #FFD400, Chart2 #69F0AE, Chart3 #FF6B6B, Chart4 #FFFFFF, Chart5 #FFD400, Chart6 #69F0AE); patterns/labels are required because color alone is never the signal.",
    "DESIGN.md does not specify TextFeatures; generated TextStyle uses ligatures/tabular_numbers/slashed_zero = false, stylistic_set = 0, and tab_size = 4 for Code.",
    "Dark BorderFocus is not named in DESIGN.md; it uses the dark FocusRing #93C5FD so the focus border and ring agree."
  ]
